      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64669,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64670,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64671,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>This tumour occurs in the uterine cervix, as well as in the uterus and the vagina. See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/259\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Adenosarcoma of the uterine corpus</em>&nbsp;and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/357\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Adenosarcoma of the vagina</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T11:09:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64672,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present across a wide age range (mean: 48&nbsp;years) but tend to be younger than patients with uterine corpus tumours {27771166}. Clinical presentations include vaginal bleeding or discharge, pelvic pain, and a mass/polyp discovered on examination {18552169; 30122564}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64673,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenosarcoma is rare. It accounts for 0.16% of all cervical cancers and approximately 10% of adenosarcomas of the female genital tract {27771166}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64674,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. No relation to HPV has been documented {18552169}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64675,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64676,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours can be polypoid/papillary or nodular and endophytic {30122564}. The median size is 3.0&nbsp;cm (range: 2.0&ndash;5.0&nbsp;cm) {27771166}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64677,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>At low-power examination, a phyllodes-like architectural pattern with intraglandular polypoid projections and periglandular stromal cuffing is typical. Benign or mildly atypical glands are frequently lined by endocervical-type epithelium, occasionally with areas of squamous differentiation. The stromal component is usually low-grade endometrial stromal or fibroblastic in appearance. Mitotic figures are usually present; however, the diagnosis can be considered in the absence of mitotic figures when typical architecture is seen {18941402}. Heterologous stromal elements (fetal-type cartilage and rhabdomyoblasts) and sex cord&ndash;like areas can be present {18941402; 8600073; 17292949; 11748995}. The sarcomatous component may overgrow the epithelial component (referred to as sarcomatous overgrowth); there may also be transformation into high-grade sarcoma {2535774; 18941402}.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes benign endometrial or cervical polyps with unusual morphology (focal phyllodes-like architecture, increased stromal cellularity surrounding glands) on the one hand and adenosarcoma with a low degree of stromal mitotic activity on the other. These lesions are much more common than adenofibroma, and a diagnosis of adenofibroma should be made with caution {25118811; 26715175; 20179434}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-08T09:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64678,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64679,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64680,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> benign or mildly atypical glands and sarcomatous, usually low-grade stroma (biphasic pattern) or periglandular stromal cuffing (phyllodes-like or cystic pattern).</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> stromal mitoses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64681,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other cervical tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64682,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>For completely resected tumours confined to the cervix, the prognosis is favourable {27771166}. Local recurrences can occur, but distant metastasis is rare. Deeper cervical wall invasion, sarcomatous overgrowth, and lymphovascular space invasion adversely affect prognosis {18941402; 8600073; 31396483}. The presence of tumour stalk is an independent protective factor for recurrence {31396483}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]